sjdevnull@yahoo.com wrote:
> Yes.  Also forbid wishing for Quest artifacts.

I prefer the suggestion elsethread that wishing for a quest artifact
summons the appropriate quest nemesis, so you must fight for the
artifact. In this case, make the Dork One more dangerous, since he has
one of the best artifacts.

> a kitted-out player.  Also, make most of them _not_ do the "teleport to
> the stairs" bit; that's interesting at first, but when everything is
> doing it then you know how to deal with it and you're just doing the
> same (boring) motions repeatedly.

How about if some monsters had a chance to 'port to the downstairs
instead of the upstairs? Would make it a little less predictable, and
also, going upstairs to a level already cleared by the player is in the
player's interest. Going downstairs to a level that might still be full
of nasties makes more sense, imho.
I daresay it wouldn't be too hard for clever players to come up with a
solution to this strategy (dig down, clear the level below then come
back up) but it would introduce a small element of uncertainty into the
situation.



